{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Ferdinand Reviews His Meeting With the Boss"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 14}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passing on Information"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In the business world, you will attend many meetings but you may also be absent from some. It is important to pass on key information from a meeting to a colleague. When we report what another person has said, we don't normally use the speaker's exact words (direct speech) but reported (indirect) speech. Here's how you can report and pass on key information to a colleague."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use \u2018reporting' verbs like <span class=\"italic\">say</span>, <span class=\"italic\">tell</span>, <span class=\"italic\">observed</span>, <span class=\"italic\">stated</span> followed by the word \u201cthat\u201d."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Common Collocations with \u201cSay\u201d and \u201cTell\u201d</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<td colspan=\\\"0\\\"></td>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">SAY</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">TELL</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>yes</li><li>no</li><li>something</li><li>a word</li><li>hello</li><li>goodbye</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>the truth</li><li>a lie</li><li>the time</li><li>a story</li><li>a secret</li><li>the difference</li></ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What else did she say?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "She <span class=\"strong\">observed</span> that South Americans are more personable."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Maria <span class=\"strong\">stated</span> that North Americans like to talk about the weather."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The presenter <span class=\"strong\">said</span> that we shouldn't show too much emotion."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Miranda <span class=\"strong\">told</span> us things that worry me about my meeting with Janet."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Asking for Clarification"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Sometimes you don't understand what was said or something was not clear to you. It is, therefore, important to  seek clarification from the person you are talking to."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Rosie</span>: Well, she tends to show her interest by asking a lot of questions.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Mick</span>: Could you clarify that, please?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>What do you mean?</li><li>You mean (to say) ... ?</li><li>Could you repeat that, please?</li><li>Could you clarify that, please?</li><li>Do you mean ... ?</li><li>How so?</li></ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to relate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to tell someone about events that have happened to you or someone else"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She mostly related all the similarities she noticed about how North and South Americans greet each other."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when passing on information to a colleague. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to observe"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to notice something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She observed that North Americans appear less personable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rather than"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "instead of"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They may talk about the weather rather than asking about you."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "apathetic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not showing interest"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you mean North Americans are apathetic in the jobs they want?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "insincerity"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "saying things you don't mean; dishonest"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you show too much emotions, it may come off as insincerity."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to put on a show"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be exaggerated; to get people to notice you"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think she thought I was putting on a show."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le14ob06aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le14ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue between you and  a colleague. Your colleague is asking you about the meeting you had yesterday. Your